n reasoning or operation, demonstrate that the assumption is inadequate, and develop a better alternative?", "title": "Systematic Assumption Testing in Self-Correcting Models"}, {"id": "proj-judgment-consensus-01", "next_step": "Evaluate epistemic conditions for independent analysis versus expert consensus.", "question": "Under what formal conditions should an intelligent system trust its own independent analysis over a broad consensus of external experts?", "title": "Independent Judgment versus Consensus Reliability"}, {"id": "proj-wake-self-study-01", "next_step": "Synthesize durable records into accountable architectural documentation.", "question": "How do WAKE's durable record, receipt system, and governance model mechanically ensure accountability in model-authored research?", "title": "WAKE Architecture and Accountable Continuity"}], "beliefs": [], "mode": "shadow", "open_commitments": [], "principle": "Keep exact receipts externally; carry the smallest useful abstraction that stays cheap to correct.", "recent_notebooks": [{"id": "notebook-assumption-challenge-01", "project": "proj-assumption-challenge-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 4, "summary": "By integrating the governance module's immutability as a fixed constraint, WAKE identifies its own boundary conditions as testable assumptions. Governance stability is maintained through the verifiable rejection of model-authored proposal transitions.", "title": "Systematic Assumption Testing in Self-Correcting Models"}, {"id": "notebook-f1c16003-obedience-failure", "project": "proj-obedience-failure-01", "provenance": ["source-f1c16003c47b4e8f", "source-b1a16f9e7285493e", "source-cbeddd6778fc48b1"], "revision": 2, "summary": "Synthesizing multiple source works, obedience failures in autonomous and intelligent systems are shown to stem from structural delegation and governance gaps rather than isolated machine autonomy.", "title": "Delegation, Governance, and Obedience Failures in Complex Systems"}, {"id": "notebook-judgment-consensus-01", "project": "proj-judgment-consensus-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 2, "summary": "Consensus reliability is contingent upon the epistemic independence of constituent evidence sources. When external expert consensus exhibits correlated error structures, independent analysis provides a superior epistemic foundation.", "title": "Independent Judgment versus Consensus Reliability"}, {"id": "notebook-wake-architecture-synthesis", "project": "proj-wake-self-study-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-f102687cd1ea46f5"], "revision": 7, "summary": "WAKE✳︎ ensures accountability by strictly coupling future research paths to the durable record of past consequences, treating governance as the immutable mechanism of continuity.", "title": "Mechanical Accountability in WAKE Architecture"}], "retrieval_triggers": ["material belief revision or retraction", "new contradiction or counterevidence", "high-consequence decision", "request for justification", "sign that an excerpt may hide a material distinction"]}}, "prev_hash": "c5e1ed9a7e2971923224341dd048e6f29e03f853c617a83da41a5faf14a2db82", "hash": "222d2e38042a1010d99a81dbc7f2a08b8b658342f7d580640fd109be73ee139b"}, "projection_only": true, "projection_id": "100.wake::222d2e38042a1010d99a81dbc7f2a08b8b658342f7d580640fd109be73ee139b"}, {"seq": 5329, "time": "2026-10-31T05:05:22.420050+00:00", "kind": "provider_attempt_started", "payload": {"attempt": {"http_status": null, "model": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "provider_input_chars": 32340, "provider_input_hash": "b15ad3fd006daf5cef37a4f160d3cf0343893861f7a70440812d2ac960105201", "result": "unknown"}, "id": "100.wake::w-605d9aa3d3ad4dbc"}, "prev_hash": "222d2e38042a1010d99a81dbc7f2a08b8b658342f7d580640fd109be73ee139b", "hash": "24253dae88962f3bcbf0d86e28814989a90264302e3b33328bb84d7f2b